  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshPro
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'In Meter''s Update, the leak takes a little from level every frame. Right after it, if (level < 0f) sets level back to 0, so the leak never pushes it below zero. A check like this, which keeps a value from becoming wrong, is called defensive.


    <b>Predict:</b> Start Level is 0.3, and the level leaks 0.1 each second. What does Level show after 10 seconds?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Press Play, select Meter 8, and watch Level.

    2. Stop Play. In Meter.cs, put // in front of level = 0f;

    3. Press Play again, and watch Level.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -6055507529455485361, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
