      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "After counting, Add One compares. != means not equal, so if (currentCount != targetCount) return; stops the method while the count is not the target. Only when the two are equal do the lines below run: onCountReached.Invoke() calls what is in the event's list, here Lamp 2 \u203A SetActive.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Target Count is 3. You click 2 \xB7 Add One four times. How many times does the line onCountReached.Invoke() run?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Press Play, select Counter 2 and open Code Watch.\n2. Click 2 \xB7 Add One, and watch onCountReached.Invoke().\n3. Stop Play, tick Reset When Reached, and try again."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
