  m_text: 'Every frame, ProximityLamp measures the distance to the visitor and compares it with range. If the distance is smaller, the if block switches the light on; otherwise the else block switches it off. As Visitor 9 walks back and forth, the two blocks take turns.


    <b>Predict:</b> You set Range to 0. Which block runs as Visitor 9 walks past the lamp?


    <b>Try:</b>

    1. Press Play, select Lamp 9 and open Code Watch.

    2. Watch Distance and the two blocks as the visitor walks.

    3. Set Range to 0, then to 5.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
